  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Atomics Aeronautical Systems recorded $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems received 119 awards so far, with an average award size of $9.7M. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations fell 29.5% year over year compared with the prior fiscal period. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems continues to sell mainly aircraft and related systems: Aircraft Manufacturing accounted for $367M, Other Support Activities for Air Transportation accounted for $315M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounted for $228M. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems work is concentrated with a few agencies: The Department of Defense obligated $846M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $314M in FY2026 to date. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems obligations in FY2026 to date are lower than several prior fiscal years including FY24 at $2.3B, FY21 at $2B, and FY22 at $1.9B, and are higher than FY25 at $1.6B. General Atomics Aeronautical Systems current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers of General Atomics Aeronautical Systems in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $846M. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $314M. The General Services Administration and the Department of the Interior show $0 in obligations in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive General Atomics Aeronautical Systems federal revenue?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market with $367M in obligations, followed by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $315M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $228M. Additional markets include Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $144M and Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $68.8M."
      }
    ]
